<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Auto-backup rules for Android 11 and below (API 29-30), where the attribute
  is `android:fullBackupContent`. Android 12+ reads data_extraction_rules.xml
  instead; the two files say the same thing and both have to, because minSdk
  is 29 and the app runs on both.

  Settings and saved networks are backed up. Nothing else is.

  The two preference files holding secrets are excluded because restoring them
  cannot work. The ciphertext is encrypted with a key in the Android Keystore, and
  a Keystore key is hardware-bound and non-exportable: it does not travel with the
  backup. So a restore onto a new phone brings back ciphertext with no key to read
  it, and flutter_secure_storage's answer to an unreadable entry is to delete it.

  Left alone, that means every saved password vanishes silently on a phone
  migration while every network survives — profiles live in plain settings and
  restore fine — so the user sees their networks exactly as before and simply
  cannot authenticate, with nothing on screen to say why.

  Excluding them makes the outcome honest instead: the password fields are
  empty on the new device, which is a thing the user can see and fix, and is
  the true state of affairs either way.

  The `file` domain is excluded for a different reason: privacy. Everything the app
  writes for itself is there, under getApplicationSupportDirectory: the message
  history, which is not encrypted, the chat and debug logs, files received from
  other people, Tor's state, and the local server's CA key. The app promises these
  stay on the device, and a backup would copy them to the user's cloud account
  without anyone having been asked. Losing them on a new phone is the cost, and it
  is the right way round: history can be left behind, and cannot be taken back.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <!-- The credentials themselves. -->
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="FlutterSecureStorage.xml"/>
    <!-- The Keystore-wrapped key that encrypts them, equally unusable once
         moved off the device that made it. -->
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="FlutterSecureKeyStorage.xml"/>
    <!-- History, logs, received files, Tor's state, the local server's key. -->
    <exclude domain="file" path="."/>
</full-backup-content>
